losslesscut (3.69.0-1foundry1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Initial Foundry Linux packaging of LosslessCut 3.69.0.
  * Repackages upstream's official self-contained Linux application bundle.
    The payload is taken from the published AppImage rather than the .tar.bz2:
    both carry the identical Electron and FFmpeg tree, but the AppImage also
    ships upstream's own 512x512 PNG icon and desktop entry, which the
    tarball omits.
  * The AppImage is unpacked at build time and its contents installed to
    /usr/lib/losslesscut. Nothing mounts an AppImage at runtime, so the
    package needs no FUSE support.
  * Bundled FFmpeg 8.0 is retained. LosslessCut resolves it relative to its
    own resources directory and the binaries are $ORIGIN-relative, so the
    tree relocates cleanly; no system ffmpeg is required or consulted.
  * Upstream ships no Debian packaging of its own -- no debian/ directory,
    no .deb build script, and no PPA, Launchpad, OBS or COPR presence. Their
    Linux distribution channels are the AppImage, the tarball, Snap and
    Flathub (no.mifi.losslesscut). The binary package name losslesscut
    matches upstream's own binary, Snap and desktop-entry naming; the
    Repology project slug is lossless-cut, recorded in X-Repology-Project.
  * chrome-sandbox is installed setuid root so Electron uses the SUID
    sandbox. Upstream's AppImage sidesteps this by launching with
    --no-sandbox; shipping the helper correctly keeps the renderer sandbox
    enabled instead.
  * The AppDir's six bundled compatibility shims under usr/lib are not
    installed. libgconf-2.so.4 needs libgconf-2-4, which no longer exists in
    26.04, and libappindicator.so.1/libindicator.so.7 are GTK2 and need
    libdbusmenu-gtk4, which has no installation candidate — their own
    dependencies are unsatisfiable on this target. libnotify.so.4,
    libXtst.so.6 and libXss.so.1 are superseded by libnotify4, libxtst6 and
    libxss1 from the archive; because Electron dlopens those three rather
    than linking them, dh_shlibdeps cannot see them and they are listed in
    Depends explicitly.

 -- Foundry Linux <packages@foundrylinux.org>  Sat, 29 Aug 2026 16:38:09 -0600
